tar
Usage: tar c|x|t [-zJjahmvokO] [-f TARFILE] [-C DIR] [-T FILE] [-X FILE] [LONGOPT]... [FILE]...

Create, extract, or list files from a tar file.

	c	Create an archive
	x	Extract
	t	List contents
	-f TARFILE	Archive file, or '-'
	-C DIR	Work inside DIR
	-v	List sizes, modes
	-O	Extract to stdout
	-m	Don't restore mtime
	-o	Don't restore user:group
	-k	Don't replace existing files
	-z	gzip (.tar.gz)
	-J	xz (.tar.xz)
	-j	bzip2 (.tar.bz2)
	--lzma	(De)compress using lzma
	-a	(De)compress based on extension
	-h	Follow symlinks
	-T FILE	Names in FILE
	-X FILE	File with glob patterns to exclude
	--exclude GLOB	Skip names matching
	--overwrite		Replace existing files
	--strip-components NUM	Drop NUM top dirs
	--no-recursion		Don't enter dirs
	--numeric-owner		Numeric uid:gid
	--no-same-permissions	Don't restore access permissions
	--to-command COMMAND	Pipe files to COMMAND
